# Playwright (Phase 15) — test artifacts and the per-run fixture manifest
# tools/src/e2e-seed.ts writes (contains a plaintext invite token, single-run
# only; never a real secret, but not something to commit either).
# Unanchored, deliberately. These were `/test-results/` and
# `/playwright-report/`, which match only at the repo root — and Playwright
# writes them relative to whatever directory it was started in. Running
# `npx playwright test` from inside `web/` produced `web/test-results/`, which
# git happily tracked and which then broke tools/src/docker-stack.test.ts by
# looking like a source directory the Dockerfile had forgotten to copy.
test-results/
playwright-report/
/e2e/.fixtures.json
